cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Frozen-horizon cosmology: pipeline, results, and manuscripts"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Pipeline for two companion papers on a metric f(R) extension of Starobinsky
  inflation possessing an exact constant-curvature solution -- a frozen
  horizon -- with a single unstable scalaron mode. Paper I covers the
  trace-flow wall and its zero-work measure, the unit spectral gap, the
  Einstein-frame background, scalar and tensor spectra integrated exactly
  through the wall, the reheating closure that fixes the feature scale, and
  propagation to the CMB with evaluation of the official Planck 2018
  low-multipole likelihoods. Paper II covers the Euclidean four-sphere
  saddle, its boundary fluctuation kernel in closed form, the classicalizing
  contour and the admissible window 7/4 < mu^2 < 4, the Neumann lapse
  contour, and the discrete S^3 mode-crossing kernel. Every table and figure
  in both manuscripts is regenerated by reproduce.sh, so no number in
  either paper is transcribed by hand.
